  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and economic integration of refugees in Jordanian communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The research aims to understand how labor market opportunities and intergroup contact affect social cohesion between Syrian refugees and Jordanians. Through a randomized evaluation of cash-for-work programs, it tests whether working in mixed Syrian-Jordanian teams and receiving information that counters stereotypes can reduce prejudice, increase trust, and improve team productivity. The study also examines whether these interventions improve income generation and longer-term employment prospects, with the goal of informing refugee employment and social-cohesion policies in Jordan and the broader region.</narrative>
  </description>
